Z||000018||JSocha||05-14-2001||12:31 PM||||Chop Top, I still think you have one cool  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> as well as fine set of wheels there!  I have Fiero Chop Top envy here!<P>Wife and I went for the Sunday drive yesterday to the parents cabin in the Fiero and I asked her what she would think of a chop top.  After explaining it to her, she says...no...you barely fit as is in this car!  I'm 5'11 (long upper body ... short legs).  Seat back rest lays way back when I drive just so I don't bank my head against the ceiling (ouch!)!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||btoth||05-14-2001||01:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>Chop Top, I still think you have one cool   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> as well as fine set of wheels there!  I have Fiero Chop Top envy here!<P>Wife and I went for the Sunday drive yesterday to the parents cabin in the Fiero and I asked her what she would think of a chop top.  After explaining it to her, she says...no...you barely fit as is in this car!  I'm 5'11 (long upper body ... short legs).  Seat back rest lays way back when I drive just so I don't bank my head against the ceiling (ouch!)!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm the exact opposite... 6' and long legs, short body.  I like to think I'm made for low cars.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
