Z||000027||pontiacs4me||05-15-2001||01:13 AM||||My friend Andy and I just made the last half of the power tour in my fiero.  I drove most of the way to san bernardino, because he is 6'8" tall and 270 lbs.  I think he only drove 180 miles on the way there.  I made him drive half of the way back, because we made the trek in 1 day.  He had to take his shoes off (size 17) for the extra leg room.  His right knee gets stuck on the front of the dash board and he has a hard time moving his foot from the gas pedal to the brake pedal.  Good thing the car is an auto, he wouldnt be able to push the clutch pedal because his left leg is so cramped also.  I am 6'2" and our upper bodies are about the same height, his legs are about 6" longer than mine.  And damn that is a long drive in a fiero.  ||||reg||1
